WEBVTT

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.760
Always to rule

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.640
In East Africa there is a valley called the Great Fertile,

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.880
which is part of one of the longest valleys in the world.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.280
On the banks of this valley,

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.230
huge mountains rise.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:22.370
To the west, the Zaire River and the wild jungle,

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.280
the heart of the continent.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.840
To the east, the vast and serene Serengeti plain.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.000
To the north, Lake Victoria

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.040
and the deep waters of the Nile, which runs through the entire desert of Egypt

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.560
to the Mediterranean Sea.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.980
For many years, Africa was known as the Black Continent.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.210
People did not know their customs and habits.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.570
Many even thought it was a mysterious and enigmatic place.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.900
But now the progress has expanded and reached the Black Continent.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:55.160
Africa, cradle and origin of the great pharaohs of Egypt,

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.890
the origin of the human species,

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.770
has now joined the modern world,

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.000
and where otherwise

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.080
that once was a jungle, are now growing into big cities.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.970
Here, in the dense tropical forest,

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:12.470
is the only place where Africa is still the mysterious and dangerous Black Continent.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:18.350
Progress, however, brought new ways of destroying and killing

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.350
to continue the battle of life and death,

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:25.240
where only the greatest and strongest survive.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.480
The animals we catch are all over blue.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.520
But I want the White Lion, that's what I'm here for.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.000
Did you hear that story about the White Lion?

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:05.480
- I doubt it exists, huh? - Ah, it does! There must be some around...

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.020
I'm close! Open the car!

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.620
I'll take what I said! There's really a white lion!

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.280
Go there! Get closer to him!

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:45.920
Closer! Don't lose sight of him in a second!

00:03:55.250 --> 00:04:00.000
Give me your gun, quick!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.440
This is private property!

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.000
Dear Anja,

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.990
I've got news for you.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.990
You'll be a dad soon.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.880
Lina, are we going to have a baby?

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.280
Yes, let's.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:13.560
Yay!

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.570
Thank you.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:23.000
It's a happy day for all of us.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.420
It seems so.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.150
Stop!

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.190
Panza! I'm glad it's you!

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.270
The monkeys are back in the bush and there's nothing or no one.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.030
One of them is seriously injured.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:42.930
I told you! No fighting between us!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:47.220
But it's not worth it, Panza! You know what it's like when they're hungry.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:50.620
There are days when there's not enough food in the jungle.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:55.920
It even scares me. I think they're capable of killing themselves to eat anything.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:59.280
Then I'll have to take other measures, Baboon Daniel.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.110
Your majesty, wait!

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.130
Is Panja here with you, Daniel?

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.130
Well, he left, Lina.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.020
Don't tell me he went to the Human Village again.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:11.970
Yes.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:17.070
But he's going to be a father soon and it's so dangerous.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:20.070
Why does he always have to take great risks? Why?

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.250
He does that for the benefit of all of us.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.130
You know that there isn't much to eat and the humans have always been kept.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:30.000
Well, I always say that he has to go, that he may not come back, but he goes anyway.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.760
I am already envious of you.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:45.590
You present yourselves as great lion hunters

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:49.140
and the only thing you do is wait against everything you eat.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.080
And the White Lion is still going free.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.080
Why do you think I hired you and sent you especially to America?

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.110
- Just allow me to... - Shut up!

00:06:56.110 --> 00:07:00.000
The people of the village are fed up with losing cattle because of that White Lion.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.280
They came to ask for help, and that's why I hired you!

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.560
Because you presented yourselves as experts in the field!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.460
But clearly, you're not the men who did it!

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:11.920
I'm very disappointed in you!

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.500
Shame on your face, man!

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.600
Maybe, sir, but I've done my best so far!

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:29.060
You're not even embarrassed, are you?

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:29.920
Well...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.100
He must be very sick, or maybe he's too old.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:36.140
He's neither old nor sick, it's just courage.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.140
He comes to get food for the other animals in the jungle.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.140
But the cat is also an animal.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:46.110
But he lives with the humans, which the others consider a betrayal.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.110
Did you hear that?

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.980
Look! There he goes!

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:53.480
Forget it, he's too far away.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:08:00.000
I have a better idea.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.840
And you there in pyjamas? What is this?

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:06.800
It's a recorder, sir. Didn't you tell us that the white lion has a companion?

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:10.800
A lioness for whom he has a great attraction. That's it, isn't it?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.630
Yes, it's possible. And then?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:18.630
I had a brilliant idea. If it turns out as well as I think, that lion has the days counted.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:30.000
And so, a few days later, the hunters arrived.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:43.220
returned to America. They had fulfilled their terrible mission.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:46.640
A great moment is almost here. What great moment?

00:08:46.640 --> 00:09:00.000
Mrs. Panja is about to give birth at any moment.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:07.500
Mr. Pan is completely alone at this difficult time, there are volunteers to help, are we men or are we...

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.500
I want it, I want it, I want it, I want it!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:19.200
Your answer was disgusting.

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:44.580
Mrs. Bunge needs privacy!

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:50.320
These buns are killing me!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.380
How many babies can a mother-of-a-lion have?

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.890
What if there are too many?

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:56.280
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:19.970
Yeah, I just wanna dance, just wanna dance, just wanna dance, ha ha ha ha!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:24.470
And I, and I, I'm walking on the street, and I, and I, I'm walking on the street, ha ha ha ha!

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.940
I'm going to the party, I'm going to the party, ha ha ha ha!

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.390
That little white lion is going to make me win a fortune.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.230
There are zoo gardens that would give a lot of money to one of those animals.

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:17.170
Then I swear to you, whether it rains or it snows...

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:21.320
Hey, buddy, I'm a meteorologist. I'm going to fly through the city of the wind.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:24.710
And because of the changes in the weather, I'm facing a great storm.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:28.130
I'm also here with the two of us in my room and I'm telling you that we're going to get out of here.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:30.000
We can't do that. We're rats.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.000
Besides that, we have Panja's son on board.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.940
Panja's son?

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.340
More news, Mrs. Panja.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.160
Hey, who's this?

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.500
See this girl here?

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.450
This must be her little father.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:53.000
We all have a father? Even me?

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.440
That's a good question.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.410
Come here, daughter, I'll tell you.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.000
Tell me what?

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.910
It's been two months since you were born, so you're not a baby anymore.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.180
You're old enough to know these things.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:12.480
Your father was called Panja, the bravest lion in the jungle, also the most generous.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.510
Always taking care of everyone, but no one could take care of him.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.840
One day, the most feared happened.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:35.000
I wasn't expecting Panja to come back so early, he went to the valley.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.950
Panja?

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:52.590
We just have to wait for him to fall right into our trap!

00:12:53.720 --> 00:13:00.000
Panja, get out of here!

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.550
They're here. Run, Panja, run away from here!

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:24.610
If your only son were a boy,

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:27.740
can you grant me a wish, my dear?

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.000
Can you call

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:31.130
Kimba?

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.320
Your father was a very noble and great lion.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:54.960
Kimba, promise me that you will always honor him in your memory.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:55.990
Yes!

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.080
Kimba, huh?

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.550
I like it!

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.000
Now, my son,

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.620
I want you to leave this ship and find the way to the jungle.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:04.820
That's where your home is.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:06.050
Alright, mom.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:09.670
And you, don't you come with me?

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:12.610
I can't. I'm stuck in this jail.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.020
You'll have to go alone.

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:24.840
No, mom, I don't want to leave you, Kimba, but you have to try to be strong like your father.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.230
It's wrong to run with a kid like that. He's a baby.

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:30.000
It's for his own good, see?

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.950
- It's a big storm. - Huh? What?

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.950
Shut up! The ship could even sink!

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:38.070
- Then why are we waiting? Let's get out of here! - No!

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.110
- Shhh! -

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:43.890
- I'm touching the cat! You know who's in power! -

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:48.850
I'm going to teach those bigwigs to mess with someone their size.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:53.060
That's the spirit, Kimba. But the animals in the jungle need a lot more of you.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:57.970
You have to go. Your place is in the jungle. You are the son of Panja.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.530
Goodbye, Kimba.

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:07.810
Goodbye, mom.

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:11.080
And don't worry, I promise I'll find the jungle.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:18.690
Be careful!

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:10.490
What happened to the big boat?

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:29.760
Mommy!

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:32.280
Wait a sec!

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:37.970
Guys, let them swim! I'm going to teach them everything they need to know!

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:43.110
I don't have a swim suit!

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:44.110
I don't either!

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.350
Give me your paws! Give me your paws!

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:51.750
As much as you can!

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.750
Don't breathe! Don't breathe!

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:57.460
Oh no!

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.240
It's super simple, you just have to spread your legs like this, see?

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:07.480
Up, down, up, down, up, you get it?

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:16.690
They still say horse-horses don't lynch, oh!

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:28.320
I don't think it's any kind of fish, maybe it's a human being!

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:30.000
Done, now we just have to...

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.020
I'm not a hero, I'm a hero.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:23.480
The son of Spongebob!

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:26.440
Oh, they're all the same, it's just a little one.

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:30.000
When the ship sank, I was worried about you.

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:32.030
But now I see that you're well.

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:36.060
Did you meet my father too, Mr. Bird?

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:41.060
Oh, Pascal, your father was my friend, and all the animals on Earth, in the sky, in the sea.

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:43.060
And you met him well.

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:49.430
I was there on that sad day when he left the jungle forever.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.420
Don't go!

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:52.320
It's obvious that it's a joke.

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:56.910
Don't you understand, Panda? Humans want to catch you, or maybe even worse.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:57.760
I know.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:00.000
But I don't have an alternative.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.500
You're right once and for all! You're our leader!

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:04.230
You have to stay with us!

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:08.360
My duty is to protect the weak and innocent.

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:12.210
Protect our safety from anyone who comes to cause trouble.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.280
My enemies are there.

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:18.050
They captured Alina. I don't care what can happen to me anymore.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:22.880
If I don't come back, my friends will have to learn to defend themselves.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:25.160
This battle is mine.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:26.500
Goodbye.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:33.040
And so he left, without ever hesitating.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:35.780
Without thinking about the dangers he could find.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:37.810
Unstopable.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.070
Fearless.

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:42.050
You must be like your father, little one.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.760
I know like the big belly.

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:46.510
Don't look back.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.740
Don't run away from your problems, don't give up.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.120
Nothing, my little one, nothing!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.580
Nothing until you get to where you want to go.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:56.400
Nothing!

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:57.380
Nothing!

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:00.000
Kima, my son, courage.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:08.440
Be strong. Your house is right here, behind the horizon. Your home.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:21.860
I'm here, Kimba. And I will always be with you.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:26.560
If I can follow them, they will take me to Earth.
